    "title": "pandas.Interval.open_left — pandas 2.3.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Interval.open_left#\n\n- Interval.open_left#\n- Check if the interval is open on the left side. For the meaning of closed and open see `Interval` .\n  - Returns:\n    - bool\n    - True if the Interval is not closed on the left-side.\n See also \n  - `Interval.open_right`\n  - Check if the interval is open on the right side.\n  - `Interval.closed_left`\n  - Boolean inverse of open_left.\n Examples >>> iv = pd.Interval(0, 5, closed='neither') >>> iv.open_left True >>> iv = pd.Interval(0, 5, closed='both') >>> iv.open_left False",
    "markdown_length": 529,
